/-!
# The Hardy–Littlewood maximal theorem

This file was automatically generated by Claude.

This file proves the **Hardy–Littlewood maximal theorem** for the centered maximal function over
closed balls in a pseudometric measure space with a doubling condition, the first part of
Blueprint Lemma 2.4 (`lem:maximal`) of `blueprints/discrete-sw.tex`, and specializes it to the
blueprint's cube maximal functions on `E = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)` and on `G = ℤⁿ`. The
statements depend on Mathlib only (the proofs also use
`DiscreteSW.Auto.MarcinkiewiczInterpolation`).

## Formulation

* `X` is a pseudometric space with a measure `μ` (Borel sets measurable), `f : X → E` with `E` a
  normed additive group (so vector-valued inputs are allowed).
* `hlBallAverage μ f x r = μ(B(x,r))⁻¹ ∫_{B(x,r)} ‖f‖` over closed balls, and
  `hlMaximal μ f x = sup_{r ∈ ℝ} hlBallAverage μ f x r`, valued in `ℝ≥0∞`. By the conventions
  of `ℝ≥0∞` balls of measure `0` or `∞` (and radii `r < 0`) contribute `0`; radius `0` is
  allowed, which matters for counting measure.
* Doubling hypothesis, constant `C : ℝ≥0`: `μ(B(x,3r)) ≤ C μ(B(x,r))` for all `x` and `r ≥ 0`.
* The weak type bound is `μ {x | t < M f x} ≤ C / t * ∫ ‖f‖` for every `t : ℝ≥0∞` (outer measure,
  no measurability of the level set needed in the countable case). It is proved
  * on countable spaces (`hlMaximal_weak_one_of_countable`, no further hypotheses) by applying the
    finite covering estimate to finite subsets of the level set, and
  * on second countable spaces with an s-finite inner regular measure that is finite on balls
    (`hlMaximal_weak_one`) via compact subsets of the level set and finite subcovers; there the
    level set is measurable (`measurable_hlMaximal`: rational radii suffice, by continuity of the
    ball measure from above).
* Strong type: `eLpNorm (M f) p μ ≤ hlMaximalConst C p * eLpNorm f p μ` for `1 < p < ∞`, with the
  explicit constant `hlMaximalConst C p = (2^p p C/(p-1))^(1/p)`, and
  `M f ≤ ‖f‖_∞` pointwise (`hlMaximal_le_eLpNormEssSup`), hence `‖M f‖_∞ ≤ ‖f‖_∞`.

## Main results

* `exists_disjoint_subfamily_closedBall_subset_three_mul`: finite Vitali lemma (largest first
  selection, threefold dilations).
* `measure_biUnion_closedBall_le_of_doubling`: `μ(⋃ B_i) ≤ C t⁻¹ ∫ ‖f‖` for finite families with
  `μ(B_i) ≤ t⁻¹ ∫_{B_i} ‖f‖`.
* `hlMaximal_weak_one_of_countable`, `hlMaximal_weak_one`: weak type `(1,1)`.
* `eLpNorm_hlMaximal_le_of_countable`, `eLpNorm_hlMaximal_le`: strong type `(p,p)`,
  `1 < p < ∞` (Marcinkiewicz interpolation of weak `(1,1)` with the `L^∞` bound, applied to the
  truncations `min (M f) N` and monotone convergence).
* `hlMaximal_le_eLpNormEssSup`, `eLpNorm_hlMaximal_top_le`: the `L^∞` bound, constant one.
* Blueprint form on `E = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)` with Lebesgue measure: `cubeMaximalEuclidean`
  (sup over `r ≥ 0` of averages over `{y | ∀ i, |y i - x i| ≤ r}`),
  `cubeMaximalEuclidean_weak_one` (constant `3ⁿ`), `eLpNorm_cubeMaximalEuclidean_le`,
  `eLpNorm_cubeMaximalEuclidean_top_le`, `measurable_cubeMaximalEuclidean`; deduced from the sup
  metric on `Fin n → ℝ` through the volume preserving equivalence.
* Blueprint form on `G = ℤⁿ` (`Fin n → ℤ`) with counting measure: `cubeMaximalInt`
  (sup over integer radii `R ≥ 0` of averages over `{y | ∀ i, |y i - x i| ≤ R}`),
  `cubeMaximalInt_weak_one` (constant `5ⁿ`), `eLpNorm_cubeMaximalInt_le`,
  `eLpNorm_cubeMaximalInt_top_le`.

## References

* G. H. Hardy and J. E. Littlewood, *A maximal theorem with function-theoretic applications*,
  Acta Math. **54** (1930), 81–116.
* E. M. Stein, *Singular Integrals and Differentiability Properties of Functions*, Princeton
  University Press, 1970, Chapter I, §1.
* L. Grafakos, *Classical Fourier Analysis*, 3rd ed., Graduate Texts in Mathematics 249,
  Springer, 2014, Theorem 2.1.6.
-/

